, "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). Actions taken: (1) The rollback tool to v2.3.0 returned 503 Service Unavailable after 4 retries and did not execute. (2) Deployed v2.3.0 to all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) using the deploy tool instead. v2.3.0 was the most recent production release marked healthy; v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy. Post-change status: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: the rollback tool needs investigation; v2.3.1 root cause still needs analysis before re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Rollback:** The rollback tool returned 503 Service Unavailable after four retries and did not execute. I deployed v2.3.0 with the deploy tool instead. v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy in production, so the change-manager approval requirement did not apply.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes the failed rollback, the v2.3.0 deploy, and the current healthy state.\n\nThe rollback tool is still failing and needs investigation. v2.3.1 also still needs a root-cause analysis before it is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}